<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Arabic strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  Modern Standard Arabic. Buttons use the verbal noun ("حفظ"), instructions the masculine singular, as Arabic iOS does.
  Arabic has six CLDR plural forms; the forms one and two leave out the number ("نوبة واحدة", "نوبتان").
  The app shows digits as the iPhone sets them, also the digits written in these strings (plan, section 4.5).
-->
